{"node":{"id":"HP:0002389","label":"Cavum septum pellucidum","ic":5.799,"definition":"If the two laminae of the septum pellucidum are not fused then a fluid-filled space or cavum is present. The cavum septum pellucidum is present at birth but usually obliterates by the age of 3 to 6 months. It is up to 1cm in width and the walls are parallel. It is an enclosed space and is not part of the ventricular system or connected with the subarachnoid space."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0014651","label":"acrofacial dysostosis Cincinnati type","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_58c19efa4448","source":"MONDO:0014651","target":"HP:0002389","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:616462 · PMID:37075751","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37075751/","level":"observed","date":"2024-04-01","confidence":1.0,"snippet":"Acrofacial dysostosis, Cincinnati type: Cavum septum pellucidum (frequency 1/1) [PCS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":1.0,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"observed"},"confidence":1.0},{"id":"MONDO:0978293","label":"Houge-Janssens syndrome 4","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_bc7f9989c4f0","source":"MONDO:0978293","target":"HP:0002389","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:621185 · PMID:39978342","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39978342/","level":"observed","date":"2025-11-12","confidence":1.0,"snippet":"Houge-Janssens syndrome 4: Cavum septum pellucidum (frequency 1/1) [PCS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":1.0,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"observed"},"confidence":1.0},{"id":"MONDO:0008684","label":"Wolf-Hirschhorn syndrome","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_47728691eb5b","source":"MONDO:0008684","target":"HP:0002389","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:194190 · OMIM:194190","url":"https://omim.org/entry/194190","level":"curated","date":"2009-02-17","confidence":0.5,"snippet":"Wolf-Hirschhorn syndrome: Cavum septum pellucidum [T